<!--
  The site is a hash router: every page lives at #/about, #/news and so on,
  which are fragments of this one URL rather than URLs of their own. A fragment
  is never sent to the server and crawlers normalise it away, so one entry is
  all a sitemap can honestly carry. Listing #/news here would not give a
  crawler a second page to fetch.
-->
